{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared golden vectors for AlcoholCalculator. Loaded by BOTH the Android (JVM)",
    "and iOS (Swift) test suites so the two implementations cannot silently diverge.",
    "Harvested from the authoritative Android unit tests. Changing a value here is a",
    "deliberate, reviewable change to health-relevant behaviour.",
    "Tolerances: grams and bac compare with an absolute epsilon of 0.001.",
    "calculateBAC integrates dose by dose: elimination runs between doses and is clamped at zero, so a gap in which the estimate reaches zero cannot be subtracted twice. The lumped form that anchored elimination at the first dose of the day underestimated a split session. The readout carries one decimal.",
    "isOverLimit(total, limit) = total > limit + 1e-6. The tolerance exists because 0.1-g values summed as binary doubles can drift above an exactly-met limit; a strict '>' would then report an exceedance the user cannot see.",
    "isDrinkDay(total) = total > 0. No tolerance: the comparison is against zero, not against a user-set limit, and grams live on a 0.1 g grid. A day of alcohol-free entries has a summary row but no alcohol, and is a dry day on every surface."
  ],
  "constants": {
    "ethanolDensity": 0.789,
    "bingeThreshold": 60.0,
    "widmarkR": 0.6,
    "beta": 0.15,
    "windowDays": 7,
    "limitEpsilon": 1e-06
  },
